:>Pat Rankin writes...
:>>(Mark Hood) writes...
:>>> (why can't one get color on a Unix system?)
:>> 
:>>     If you build for TERMINFO instead of TERMCAP, and if your TERMINFO
:>>database contains color entries, then you _can_ use color on Unix by
:>>setting both the 'color' and 'standout' options at run-time.
:
:i'm running hack on an SGI Iris machine
:running AT&T SYSV unix.  checking on config.h,
:TERMINFO is defined.  i have "color" and 
:"standout" in my options.
:
:i still don't get color.  either i don't 
:have color entries in my TERMINFO database
:(how do i check this?), or else something
:else is wrong.

	You need to define TEXTCOLOR  - I think this is in "unixconf.h" - as
well. Also your terminfo entries must contain color information for the
terminal you're using - this is often not the case.

